    },
    {
      "text": "Assumption 3 is related to the standard boundedness condition for importance weights in",
      "bbox": [
        58.05120849609375,
        296.98785400390625,
        443.60577392578125,
        306.2231750488281
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "classical importance sampling. The results in equations (26) and (27) have been established very",
      "bbox": [
        48.08860778808594,
        308.9429626464844,
        443.6046142578125,
        318.17828369140625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "early on in the literature; see for example Del Moral (2004). However, these results are rather",
      "bbox": [
        48.08860778808594,
        320.8980712890625,
        443.5987854003906,
        330.1333923339844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "weak since C.P/ and D.P/ are typically exponential functions of P. Assumption 4 imposes",
      "bbox": [
        48.08860778808594,
        332.8531799316406,
        443.6087951660156,
        342.0885009765625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "a practically realistic pattern of dependence on the components of X1:P, namely a forgetting",
      "bbox": [
        48.088623046875,
        344.80828857421875,
        443.6090087890625,
        355.1886901855469
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "property, which turns out to be beneﬁcial in that it mitigates the propagation of error in the",
      "bbox": [
        48.09088134765625,
        356.76397705078125,
        443.60302734375,
        365.9992980957031
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SMC algorithm. As a result the linear bounds in expression (28) can be established (Cérou",
      "bbox": [
        48.09088134765625,
        368.7190856933594,
        443.6051025390625,
        377.95440673828125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "et al. (2008) and personal communication with Professor Pierre Del Moral). As discussed in",
      "bbox": [
        48.09088134765625,
        380.6741943359375,
        443.6111755371094,
        389.9095153808594
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "more detail in the next sections these results have direct implications on the performance of",
      "bbox": [
        48.090885162353516,
        392.6293029785156,
        443.60614013671875,
        401.8646240234375
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "PMCMC algorithms. In particular expression (28) suggests that approximations of idealized",
      "bbox": [
        48.090885162353516,
        404.58441162109375,
        443.60498046875,
        413.8197326660156
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "algorithms requiring exact samples from π.dx1:P/ by algorithms which instead use a particle",
      "bbox": [
        48.090885162353516,
        415.70263671875,
        443.6090393066406,
        426.9197692871094
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "X1:P drawn from ˆπN.dx1:P/ in equation (21) are likely to scale linearly with increasing dimen-",
      "bbox": [
        48.09088134765625,
        426.3934631347656,
        443.609130859375,
        439.3794860839844
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "sions under assumption 4. This should be contrasted with the typical exponential deterioration",
      "bbox": [
        48.090087890625,
        440.4502868652344,
        443.6072998046875,
        449.68560791015625
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "of performance of classical IS approaches.",
      "bbox": [
        48.090087890625,
        452.4054260253906,
        225.20513916015625,
        461.6407470703125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "4.2.",
      "bbox": [
        48.090087890625,
        486.2583312988281,
        64.70771026611328,
        495.4737243652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "The particle independent Metropolis–Hastings update",
      "bbox": [
        73.57442474365234,
        486.2583312988281,
        309.4688415527344,
        495.4737243652344
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "To sample from π.x1:P/, we can suggest a PIMH sampler which is an IMH sampler using an",
      "bbox": [
        48.090087890625,
        497.4961242675781,
        443.60772705078125,
        508.71319580078125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "SMC approximation ˆπN.dx1:P/ of π.x1:P/ as proposal distribution. The algorithm is similar to",
      "bbox": [
        48.090476989746094,
        508.186767578125,
        443.6117248535156,
        520.6682739257812
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "the algorithm that was discussed in Section 2.4.1 where P =T and where we substitute ˆπN.dx1:P/",
      "bbox": [
        48.09063720703125,
        520.1419677734375,
        443.6114501953125,
        532.6234741210938
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "and ˆZN respectively in place of ˆpθ.dx1:T |y1:T / and ˆpθ.y1:T /, with the notation given in equation",
      "bbox": [
        48.09124755859375,
        530.5823364257812,
        443.6077880859375,
        545.2872314453125
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "(21).",
      "bbox": [
        48.090576171875,
        546.1539916992188,
        67.38813781738281,
        555.3893432617188
      ],
      "direction": [
        1.0,
        0.0
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Given .X1:P, ˆZN/, the PIMH update consists of running an SMC algorithm targeting π.x1:P/",
      "bbox": [
        58.05317687988281,
        554.0848388671875,
